SlothClash core patch 0037: XHTTP packet-up keeps several uploads in flight.

mihomo waits for the response of every packet-up upload before it sends the
next one, so upload speed is capped at one sc-max-each-post-bytes per round
trip plus sc-min-posts-interval-ms. Like Xray's client, the writer now starts
the next upload once the headers of the previous one are written, and paces
uploads (not writes) by sc-min-posts-interval-ms. Uploads wait for their
response in a window of 8 seqs: seq N starts only once seq N-8 has been
answered, so a server never holds more than 7 uploads ahead of the one it waits
for, within the default sc-max-buffered-posts (30) of Xray, mihomo and Citrus.
A failed upload fails the next Write and aborts the others; Close waits up to
1 s for the uploads in flight. With `alpn: [http/1.1]` every upload still waits
for its response. The server side is unchanged: mihomo's listener already puts
uploads back in order by seq.

The code is the same as ClashFest core patch 0038 (Nemu-x/ClashFest#295,
GPL-3.0), only the patch number in comments differs, so the two clients stay in
sync. The seq window follows Rerowros/veles (v1.19.33-veles.3, P5/P8,
transport/xhttp/client.go, GPL-3.0); the HTTP/1.1 exception follows
getmikan/Citrus (transport/xhttp/client.go, GPL-3.0). Tests in
packet_up_pipelining_test.go (helpers after Veles' packet_up_veles_test.go).

